fy while Buffy the  Vampire Slayer might have ended years  ago the iconic name of one of our  favorite characters lives on Andy max  the even stated that she got named after  the Vampire Slayer although we have a  feeling it'll be extremely hard to fill  in the cool shoes that were once worn by  the original Buffy it's important to  note this adorable tribute so why is  this show changing Disney Channel well  for one because Disney never touched on  the coming on issue so directly while  there might have been plenty of  subliminal messages that could have been  directed at the LGBT youth and Emax  characters have made history by  addressing one of the most important  things LGBTQ teens face today  Cyrus even talks to Buffy about feeling  different and weird  - which Buffy replies that he has always  been weird just never different they're  comforting words are words that many  LGBTQ teens need to hear touching on  issues like this gives this particular  Disney show a brand new meaning for many  and shows that they are finally getting  to know their demographic in the past a  lot of Disney shows focused on  presenting the struggles teens face  every day but they were always  one-dimensional and never touched on  sexuality and since teenagers often know  about their sexuality from a young age  it's extremely important to have a  Disney show that finally addresses these  issues and show support but Andy Mack  isn't only as support for the LGBT youth  the show also touches an area that isn't  really talked about much and that is  military families in the story Buffy's  mother returns home from the military  and the story itself even resonated with  the actress that plays Buffy as her  father was part of a military family  when the episode was first screened the  cast had the privilege of doing a  private screening with military families  in New York this shows the importance  that no matter what your story is it's  meant to be heard whether your family  circumstances are different from others  or whether you as a person feel like  you're different from others your story  is meant to be listened to and most  importantly it highlights the fact that  whatever you might be going through  you're never alone there's even more to  it coming-of-age might look different in  different cultures and religions which  is why Andy Mack awesome highlights the  Jewish culture as one of the characters  has a Bar Mitzvah even the cast's are  able to draw from their own stories  Joshua rush who plays Cyrus was able to  use some of his personal items during  that bar mitzvah episode including a  tallit that was given to him by his  grandparents  Disney might not have a really bright  past when it comes to educating kids on  religion but we have a feeling their  sense of humor might have shifted in a  completely different direction with Andy  Mack critical acclaim  Andy Mac has an impressive score of 88  percent on Rotten Tomatoes  and has so far been nominated once for  outstanding kids and family programming  with the coming out story in season two  premiere and Emax reputation reached  brand new heights the season 2 premiere  increased the viewership by an  impressive 72 percent and was seen by  1.1 million kids aged between 6 and 14  the story is praised as it represents  the lives of the LGBTQ youth around the  country as well as around the world  given the popularity of the show this  might mean that Disney will finally  start paying attention to the social  issues kids face in everyday life and  produce more content that might change  people's lives season three with the  popularity of season two the show has of  course been renewed for the third season  but before the launch of the third  season the show will air season two B  which should appear on screens in summer  of 2018 season 3 will reportedly be  aired in late 2018 or early 2019 not  much has been revealed on the plot and  storyline of the next season but we have  a feeling the team behind Andy Mac will  work hard to make sure that the  heartwarming stories they feature still  resonate with whatever the teenagers are  facing in their everyday life and we  feel like we definitely won't be  disappointed considering what we have  seen so far and that's all for our video  don't forget to subscribe to the thanks  and tell us how you felt about this  video thanks for watching see you next  time  [Music]

